---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectLinks from '../components/ProjectLinks.astro';
---
<BaseLayout>
  <div class="shell simple-page">
    <article class="plain-content">
      <p>I live in Seattle and work on AI agents in <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/">Visual Studio Code</a> and <a href="https://github.com/features/copilot">GitHub Copilot</a> at Microsoft. I focus on agent products, evaluation, and OpenTelemetry-based observability.</p>

      <p>My public work includes <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/agents/guides/monitoring-agents">agent monitoring in VS Code</a>, <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/enterprise/ai-settings#_configure-telemetry-export-with-opentelemetry">enterprise telemetry export</a>, and an analysis of <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/blogs/2026/06/19/what-50000-runs-taught-us">what 50,000 repeated agent-evaluation runs taught us</a>. The <a href="https://opentelemetry.io/blog/2026/genai-observability/">official OpenTelemetry GenAI walkthrough</a> uses VS Code instrumentation I worked on together with the Aspire Dashboard’s GenAI visualizer.</p>

      <p>I’m currently building <strong>OTelux</strong>, a local-first telemetry workbench for developers and coding agents; <strong>Deskpal</strong>, verified computer use for Linux desktop applications; and <strong>pi-otel</strong>, vendor-neutral OpenTelemetry instrumentation for the Pi coding agent. Their repositories will become public with their initial releases.</p>

      <p>I also build learning projects. <span class="project-name">Learn C</span><ProjectLinks repository="https://github.com/b1tank/learnc" demo="https://b1tank.github.io/learnc/" label="Learn C" /> is a hand-written, runnable companion to K&amp;R, and <span class="project-name">Learn Ghostty</span><ProjectLinks repository="https://github.com/b1tank/learn-ghostty" demo="https://b1tank.github.io/learn-ghostty/" label="Learn Ghostty" /> is a visual, source-backed path through terminal architecture.</p>

      <p>Other projects include <span class="project-name">OpenSnipping</span><ProjectLinks repository="https://github.com/b1tank/opensnipping-web" demo="https://b1tank.github.io/projects/opensnipping/demo/" label="OpenSnipping" />, <span class="project-name">OpenMathBoard</span><ProjectLinks repository="https://github.com/b1tank/openmathboard" demo="https://lezhi.school" label="OpenMathBoard" />, <span class="project-name">BoringBlog</span><ProjectLinks repository="https://github.com/b1tank/boringblog" demo="https://lezhiweng.com" label="BoringBlog" />, and <span class="project-name">ABC Balloon</span><ProjectLinks repository="https://github.com/b1tank/abc" demo="https://b1tank.github.io/projects/abc/demo/" label="ABC Balloon" />. I publish reusable <a href="https://github.com/b1tank/skills">AI-agent skills</a> for the coding tools and workflows I use.</p>

      <p>Before developer tools, I worked on cloud infrastructure, distributed tracing, and Azure Managed Grafana. My route into software began in chemical engineering and scientific computing, including a <a href="https://github.com/b1tank/coag">C++ aerosol model</a> that ran 90% faster than its legacy Fortran implementation.</p>

      <p>Outside work, I enjoy basketball, billiards, and studying how Stephen Curry makes impossible geometry look routine.</p>

    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
